include g474.tdc
diagram e-slow "ISR → thread, slow mode (80 %): the slice reset reprograms SysTick"
letter "E slow"
new
num value "1582 cycles"
num share "80 %"
num path "wrapped ISR, k_sem, defaults"
num arch "PendSV (USE_SWITCH=n)"
what "The same path as the fast mode, with one more step. The new slice timeout of the woken thread is the first timeout, so the driver programs SysTick again, inside the ISR and with interrupts masked. This adds 313 cycles. The dashed cursor shows where the fast mode ends (card E fast)."
evidence "Two exact modes, 304 to 313 cycles apart, with the same split (20 % / 80 %) for all five kernel objects."
evidence "TIMESLICING=n: one mode at 694 cycles. So time slicing costs about 890 cycles in this mode."
evidence "USE_SWITCH=y adds 247 to 310 cycles per wake, and 566 cycles to the IRQ max (2187 against 1621): the longest masked section is longer (cards E-sw)."
evidence "Object cost against sem (p50): fifo +86, msgq +131, event +280, poll +355 cycles."
src "wake-isr-1m/20261029T064014Z, wake-anchors-1m/20261029T014607Z"

axis "cycles after the edge" -100..1750

idle sleep -100..4 "WFI"
mask -100..9 "PRIMASK"

at 0
@edge
hw     60 "entry" : Pin, EXTI, NVIC, wake-up, exception entry, _isr_wrapper. Cold cache.
dev    26 : The ISR reads TIM2->CNT: time stamp 1 (IRQ p50 86).
@stamp1 "stamp 1"
@fast ref "fast mode" at stamp1+1269
dev    250 "k_sem_give()" : The ISR gives the semaphore. The kernel makes the waiting thread ready. update_cache() selects it as the next thread (kernel/sched.c:172-176).
dev    575? "slice reset" : The same slice reset as in the fast mode (card E fast). The split between this code and the switch path is not measured.
@r0 anchor
dev    313! "SysTick reprogram" : The new slice timeout is the first timeout, so z_add_timeout() calls sys_clock_set_timeout() (kernel/timeout.c:225-233), and the driver programs SysTick again. 313 cycles: the distance of the two modes, measured.
@r1 anchor
hw     10 : Tail-chaining into PendSV.
@pendsv anchor
pendsv 378 "switch idle → thread" : z_arm_pendsv: save the idle thread, take the woken thread from the ready queue cache (with BASEPRI), program the MPU stack guard, restore the woken thread. Length: an estimate (card E fast).
waker  56 : The thread returns from z_swap() and k_sem_take() and reads TIM2->CNT: time stamp 2.
@stamp2 "stamp 2"

mask 155..1224 "BASEPRI" : The give, the slice reset and the reprogram run with the scheduler lock and the timeout lock held (card E fast).
mask pendsv+20..pendsv+50? "BASEPRI" : z_arm_pendsv sets BASEPRI at swap_helper.S:123 and restores the BASEPRI of the woken thread (0) at swap_helper.S:270, before the MPU reprogram (bl z_arm_configure_dynamic_mpu_regions, :305). The length is not measured: an estimate from the number of instructions.

span edge..stamp1 "86" !
span stamp1..stamp2 "1582, measured" !
span r0..r1 !
